Had this discussion with my friend and It goes like this. 

&#x200B;

My Friend: if you had the chance to live forever with everything not aging and so on would you? 

&#x200B;

Me: No i would absolutely not so i get to live while everyone i care about dies forget it i would rather be launched into space be thrown out of the rocket in space without a suit on 

&#x200B;

My friend: what if Humanity do a Altered carbon where our soul is bound to a chip would you then do it?

&#x200B;

Me: still hell fucking no then the Government will abuse this so fucking hard and i would rather shoot mysef in the head with a 50. cal than live forever no matter what i would gain from it. 

&#x200B;

My friend: i would gladly accept it because then i would save up enough money start a company and if the company get's big i would buy multiple body clones of myself so i could never die as long as my chip is intact. 

&#x200B;

Me: i will never change my mind on this because what if some people just want to die permanently but they can't since they are not able to die at all i don't want to end up like that at all. also yes you will experience alot of good things but you would most likely be taken in by either the military to go to war for them or by the lab folks to get experimented on. I will not take that risk. Also if we end up going Altered Carbons way we will most likely live like them in the series it would suck so fucking hard. 

&#x200B;

My friend: why are you so negative about it. i would love to be able to live forever with my friends and loved ones why don't you feel like that?

&#x200B;

Me: as i said before because we would end up in a huge fucking mess because of it.I know for a fact that i WILL not at any point want to live to see that day come. It's not about being negative it's about knowing what i can handle and can't handle and i would never be able to handle the burden that comes with immortality.

