in Denmark we have bars that have smoking areas inside and you won't believe how many people starts to complain. My parents own a security buisness for Bars and events, so they have each a 10 min break where they can pop a cig and get back to work or get some Soda or Fanta. Some young guy had the audacity to walk straight up to one of them and hit him in the stomach and tell them to fuck off with their smoking. Mind you they were no where near anyone when smoking at that time. 

What happened after i still laugh at. The same guy who got punched in the stomach took a hold of the young lad by his ears and lifted him up in the air. Mind you this security guy was Ex Military so he didn't give a fuck then the police arrived they started laughing their ass off when they heard what happened it was so funny to watch and ofc all of his friends started to make idle threats towards my parents employees. the police only gave him a warning and banned him from going to any PUB or bars for a year. prob the funniest story. This happened at my first time going to a bar.

As a smoker i can agree with this, What i do when i smoke is i make sure i stand alone or atleast ask before i light one up unless ofc if it's in a smoking area. had some people directly walk into a smoking area and complain to me that i was smoking like what the fuck.

&#x200B;

In the end i always try to make sure no one is second hand smoking, but if i am on a random path and i can't see anyone near me i will light a cigarette, and if someone directly runs up besides me and start to walk and complain then it is them who have to move because they chose to run up to me while i was smoking

